Report #127, part 2 (user: "fix existing items that are broken too"):

Backfill secondary stats onto attunement rows banked BEFORE the #111
secondary columns existed. Those rows have correct primaries but all-zero
secondaries, and the login repair skipped them because its only trigger
was a primary deficit -- 664 of Fup's 670 rows, 11,009 templates affected
realm-wide.

The login repair (RepairUnderbankedAbsorb) now has a second trigger: the
template carries secondaries (ReadBaseStats.SecondaryTotal() > 0) but the
row's secondary columns are all zero. It rewrites the row with
ReadBaseStats' current numbers -- exactly what AttuneItemEntry banks
today -- so no drift vs a fresh attune.

Deliberately NOT touched: suffix-only rows (e.g. Vigorous Belt 51959,
Tumultuous Necklace). Their secondaries were suffix rolls whose amounts
live on the item instance (AllocationPct x suffixFactor); with the item
spent, the instance is gone and the honest value is unknowable from the
template, which has zero stats. Those keep zero and can be re-earned by
attuning another copy -- same policy as the original #111 migration note.

Touches: modules/mod-living-gear/src/LivingGear.cpp only (repair trigger).
No schema change, no wire change.
